---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import {APP_URL, DESIGN_URL, GITHUB_URL} from "@/data/env";
import {PANEL_ACCENT} from "@brewdocs.beer/design";
---
<Layout title="About BrewDocs">
    <main
        class="min-h-screen w-screen flex flex-col items-center px-6 pt-24 pb-16 lg:pt-28"
        style="background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-base-200) 85%, transparent) 65%, var(--color-base-300) 100%);">
        <h1 class="mt-5 text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About BrewDocs</h1>

        <div class="mt-8 lg:max-w-screen-md text-left flex flex-col gap-4">
            <p class="px-5">
                BrewDocs is a homebrewer's handbook and brew-day app. It sets out to digitize
                brew-day note-taking with a variety of tools built for the way brewing actually
                goes, and puts a search over an aggregated collection of brewing facts behind
                them, so a last-minute change is a quick lookup rather than a guess.
            </p>

            <div class={PANEL_ACCENT}>
                <div class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Where it is now</div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-base">
                    BrewDocs is pre-alpha. The basics are tracked — recipes, batches, and the
                    notes that go with them — but the information is more demonstrative than
                    complete, and the organizational side of it is still limited.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="px-5">
                <div class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Where it's going</div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-base">
                    The goal is comprehensive brew-day note-taking across a variety of styles and
                    processes, guided walkthroughs for taking on a style you haven't brewed
                    before, and a high-quality knowledge base behind all of it.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="px-5">
                <p>
                    If you brew, I'd like to hear from you, whether it's something you wish it did,
                    a rough edge on brew day, or just an idea worth kicking around.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3">
                    If the build side is your thing, the <a href={GITHUB_URL} class="link link-primary">GitHub</a> is public and the <a href={DESIGN_URL} class="link link-primary">design system</a> is
                    published as its own live Storybook.
                </p>
                <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                    <a href={APP_URL} class="btn btn-primary">Try the demo</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
